# devices: iphone ipad
# The remote display fills the pane. Two rows of chrome: the header (Close on
# the leading side, the computer picker centred, More and the window size on
# the trailing side) and one control row under the picture. Nothing fades:
# the header buttons are still there, and take a first tap, after an idle wait.
# Synthetic transport. `check-layout computer` runs check-computer-layout.py on
# the live tree at each state, on every device the scenario covers: the picture
# fills the pane, one control row, the picker centred between Close and More,
# nothing clipped.
launch --fixture read-preview --fixture send-preview --fixture computer-session-available-fixture
wait --id computer-status-pill --timeout 30
tap --id computer-status-pill
wait --id computer-session-more --timeout 20
wait --id computer-session-window-buttons --timeout 5
check-layout computer
shot computer-header-watching
pause 6
assert --id computer-session-window-buttons
assert --id computer-session-more
assert --id computer-session-connection-picker
check-layout computer
shot computer-header-after-idle
wait --id computer-session-control-active --timeout 15
assert --id computer-session-window-buttons
check-layout computer --controlling
shot computer-header-controlling
wait --id computer-session-more --timeout 10
